# 11. GLOBAL HEADING ANIMATION SYSTEM

Use the pinned library:

`spring-text-engine@0.1.5` and its peer dependency `@react-spring/web`.

Install only if compatible with the actual project and not already installed.

All animated heading effects in this section must use spring-text-engine and its spring-driven behavior. Do not recreate these specific text effects with CSS keyframes, CSS transitions, or Framer Motion.

Apply a suitable effect to existing headings from `h1` through `h6`, including public pages and application pages, without changing their semantic heading level.

**Important:** Do not run multiple text animations on the same heading. Choose one appropriate effect based on the heading's role. Keep headings readable, accessible, and stable during route changes.

### A. Hero headline — Skew In

Use the Skew In effect for the main public hero headline.

```tsx
import TextEngine from "spring-text-engine";

<TextEngine
  tag="h1"
  mode="once"
  letterOut={{ opacity: 0, skewX: 16, y: 14 }}
  letterIn={{ opacity: 1, skewX: 0, y: 0 }}
  letterConfig={{ tension: 240, friction: 20 }}
  letterStagger={30}
>
  Turn Industrial Byproducts Into Valuable Resources.
</TextEngine>
```

Preserve the exact numeric spring configuration. Ensure the animated element does not overflow its layout or produce horizontal scrolling.

### B. Major section headings — Unblur Lines

For appropriate major section headings, use the line-based effect:

```tsx
<TextEngine
  tag="h2"
  mode="once"
  lineOut={{ opacity: 0, filter: "blur(10px)" }}
  lineIn={{ opacity: 1, filter: "blur(0px)" }}
  lineConfig={{ tension: 190, friction: 26 }}
  lineStagger={90}
>
  Industrial Resource Intelligence
</TextEngine>
```

### C. Selected dashboard and module headings — Soft Focus

Use the word-based effect selectively on high-value module headings:

```tsx
<TextEngine
  tag="h2"
  mode="once"
  wordOut={{ opacity: 0, filter: "blur(10px)" }}
  wordIn={{ opacity: 1, filter: "blur(0px)" }}
  wordConfig={{ tension: 180, friction: 24 }}
  wordStagger={60}
>
  Assess Material Compatibility
</TextEngine>
```

### D. Small card and dialog headings — Fade Letters

Use a subtle letter fade for selected short headings:

```tsx
<TextEngine
  tag="h3"
  mode="once"
  letterOut={{ opacity: 0 }}
  letterIn={{ opacity: 1 }}
  letterConfig={{ tension: 150, friction: 24 }}
  letterStagger={34}
>
  Evidence Review
</TextEngine>
```

### Text-engine requirements

- Match the animated property value types between `Out` and `In`.
- Never use `mode="manual"`.
- Use the library's correct centering behavior when centering is needed.
- Preserve the original semantic heading level.
- Preserve stable layout dimensions and avoid cumulative layout shift.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences; provide an immediate or static equivalent where appropriate.
- Prevent animation replays on every minor state update.
- Avoid animating every heading simultaneously in a large dashboard.
- Keep body copy static, as requested.
- Do not apply blur animation to form labels, table cells, technical measurements, accessibility text, or frequently changing status messages.
- If the installed package API differs from the supplied examples, inspect the pinned version's documentation and implement the supported API instead of guessing.

